## Find |EB|
$E$ is the midpoint of $[AB]$, which has length 30.
|EB| &= \frac{30}{2}
&= 15
## Find |EC| using Pythagoras in triangle EBC
|EC|^2 &= 15^2 + 30^2
&= 1125
|EC| &= 15\sqrt{5}
## Use similar triangles
Triangles $EOB$ and $EBC$ both have a right angle (at $O$ and at $B$) and share the angle at $E$, so they are similar.
\frac{|EO|}{|EB|} &= \frac{|EB|}{|EC|}
## Solve for |EO|
|EO| &= \frac{15 \times 15}{15\sqrt{5}}
&= \frac{15}{\sqrt{5}}
&= \frac{15\sqrt{5}}{5}
&= 3\sqrt{5}
ANSWER: |EO| = 3\sqrt{5} \text{ cm}

## Find the distance from P1 to O
$P_1O$ is the hypotenuse of a right-angled triangle with both legs $10$ km.
|P_1O| &= \sqrt{10^2 + 10^2}
&= \sqrt{200}
&= 14.142\ldots\ \text{km}
&= 14\,142\ \text{m}
## Divide by the speed of sound
Time $=\dfrac{\text{distance}}{\text{speed}}$.
T &= \frac{14\,142}{343}
&= 41.2\ldots
&\approx 41\ \text{seconds}
ANSWER: T \approx 41\ \text{seconds}

## Get the square root on its own
\frac{\sqrt{100+d^2}}{0.343} &= \frac{2d}{0.255}
\sqrt{100+d^2} &= \frac{2(0.343)d}{0.255}
\sqrt{100+d^2} &= \frac{686}{255}d
## Square both sides
100 + d^2 &= \left(\frac{686}{255}\right)^2 d^2
100 + d^2 &= 7.2371\,d^2
## Collect the d² terms
100 &= 7.2371\,d^2 - d^2
100 &= 6.2371\,d^2
## Solve for d
d^2 &= \frac{100}{6.2371}
&= 16.03\ldots
d &= \sqrt{16.03\ldots}
&\approx 4.0\ \text{km}
ANSWER: d \approx 4.0\ \text{km}

## Count the pairs that sum to 101
The pairs are $1+100,\ 2+99,\ \ldots,\ 50+51$. There are 50 of them.
## Count all possible pairs
\binom{300}{2} &= \frac{300 \times 299}{2}
&= 44\,850
## Divide
P &= \frac{50}{44\,850}
&= \frac{1}{897}
ANSWER: \frac{1}{897}

## Simplify the power of a power
Multiply the indices: $(a^m)^n = a^{mn}$.
(3^4)^5 &= 3^{4 \times 5}
&= 3^{20}
## Divide the powers
Subtract the indices: $a^m \div a^n = a^{m-n}$.
\frac{3^{20}}{3^6} &= 3^{20 - 6}
&= 3^{14}
ANSWER: 3^{14}

## Find where the slope is negative
$u'(x)$ is negative where the graph is going downhill.
The graph falls after its peak near $x = 5.5$, so $x = 8$ works. (The marking scheme accepts any $x > 5$.)
## Draw the tangent at (4, 2)
Mark $(4, 2)$. Draw a straight line touching the curve there without crossing it.
The line passes through $(2, 1)$ and $(6, 3)$.
## Find the slope of the tangent
Slope $=\frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1}$.
u'(4) &\approx \frac{3 - 1}{6 - 2}
&= \frac{2}{4}
&= \frac{1}{2}
ANSWER: x = 8 \text{ (any } x > 5), \quad u'(4) \approx \frac{1}{2}
